    "offices": {
      "National Council": "The 200 members are elected for four years in the 26 cantons, each a constituency with seats apportioned by population: open-list proportional representation where a canton has several seats, plurality where it has one. It has the same powers as the Council of States, so laws and the budget need both chambers.",
      "Council of States": "The 46 members represent the cantons, two for each canton and one for each half-canton, elected under cantonal law, mostly by majority vote with a run-off (Jura and Neuchâtel use proportional representation). It has the same powers as the National Council, and the two chambers sit together as the Federal Assembly to elect the Federal Council."
    }
